Jenkins (or more precisely, the ssh-credentials plugin + Java/libcrypto) does not reliably support ED25519 private keys, especially when used with passphrases.

Key points:

ED25519 private keys use the new OpenSSH format by default (-----BEGIN OPENSSH PRIVATE KEY-----) with bcrypt KDF for passphrases.

Jenkins’ ssh-credentials plugin relies on Java’s crypto libraries, which cannot read this format.

That’s why you keep getting the error in libcrypto error.

RSA keys in PEM format (-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----) are fully supported, with or without passphrase.

Other formats:

DSA: obsolete, do not use.

ECDSA: might work, but compatibility is less certain than RSA PEM.
